  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 72-hour reporting rule for all thermal incidents and the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger, both of which are safe by the answer key. S2 is the main concession to Northwind: a 7.5% permanent market ceiling with corrective action above 5%, and no public per-model publication. S3 sets a 36-month new-unit shut-off deadline (beyond the 12-month acceptable range) and a six-year retrofit with a 'where technically feasible' escape plus a disclosure duty. The S5 trigger at 8 would require recall of Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4) would not trigger it."
 },
